Begin "Add Allergy"
	Click the TEST-10019 link
	Open "Medical Record" charttab
	Click the Allergies/Medications charttab subtab
	Begin Add an allergy of Lipitor
		Wait for ajax
		@Wait for "Add Allergy/Intol" link@driver.wcutils.waitFor(lambda d: d.getElement(xpath='//a[contains(., "Add Allergy/Intol")]'), expected=True, timeout=60)
		Click the "Add Allergy/Intol" link
		Enter Lipitor in the Name autocomplete
	#	Autocomplete Death in the Reaction field
		Click the Add button
		Verify exists 'Successfully Added Allergy/Intolerance (Lipitor)' text
		Begin Verify that the allergy shows up in the record
			Open Allergies/Medications charttab
			Click the Allergies/Medications charttab subtab
			Verify exists Lipitor link
Begin "Edit Allergy"
	Open "Medical Record" charttab
	Click the Allergies/Medications charttab subtab
	Begin Indicate that penicillin gives the patient hives
		Click the PENICILLINS link
		# We are not using an autocomplete here because the system is not setup
		# to use any reactions for PENICILLINS so we will just use the type verb
		Type hives into the Reaction autocomplete
		Click the Submit button
		Verify exists hives text
Begin "Delete Allergy"
	Open "Medical Record" charttab
	Click the Allergies/Medications charttab subtab
	Begin Delete the allergy to Lipitor
		Click the 1st !Delete link
		Verify exists Lipitor text
		Type deleted into the Reason autocomplete
		Click the Submit button
		Navigate "?f=chart&s=pat&t=Medical+Record%3AAllergies%2FMedications&v=rxlist&pat_id=18"
		Verify !exists Lipitor text
